    <sys:String x:Key="CAD_Fit_Algorithm_Desc">Algorithm: Least-squares circle fitting through 4 angle positions to calculate rotation center (Mox, Moy) and fit radius.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="CAD_Fit_Principle">Principle: 4-point circle equation (x-Mox)²+(y-Moy)²=R², solving for optimal center coordinates minimizing residual sum of squares.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="CAD_Fit_Note">Note: FitRadius should be &lt;1mm indicating high fitting accuracy. If too large, recalibrate the 4-point positions.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="CAD_Formula_Theta">θ = atan2(dy_target, dx_target) − atan2(dy_base, dx_base)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="CAD_Formula_Alpha">α = atan2(y2−y1, x2−x1)  (segment direction angle)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="CAD_Formula_DyDx">dx = x2−x1 , dy = y2−y1  (segment vector components)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="CAD_Formula_Atan2_Range">atan2 return range: (−π, π], i.e. (−180°, 180°]</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="CAD_Formula_RelativeY">dy = Ym − Moy</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="CAD_Formula_RotateX">X_final = dx·cosθ − dy·sinθ + Mox</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="CAD_Formula_RotateY">Y_final = dx·sinθ + dy·cosθ + Moy</sys:String>
